            <ArticleTitle>[Painless hysterectomy: an innovative technique].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>375-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a completely innovative approach to vaginal hysterectomy where the surgeon and anesthetist work in tandem to ensure that the patient receives optimal pain management: combined use of general and long-acting local-regional anesthesia and use of the &quot;bi-clamp&quot; procedure for bipolar electrosurgery which has proved to be a significant technical improvement. In this way, pain, until now the major drawback of this procedure, is really decreased allowing a better acceptance of the procedure and a greatly improved quality of life.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
